{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Footstep: snow",
  "description": "One step in ankle-deep cold snow on a still winter day. No impact at all: the boot presses down over 180 ms and the snow compacts with a creaking, squeaking crunch that swells as the weight comes on and stops when the foot is down; under it a soft muffled whumpf; then 60 ms of fine crystals falling back into the print. Close, dead, no echo: snow swallows everything. Use the variations for a walk.",
